From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: ITextPara duplicates, IsEqual, CanChange, Reset (3606)

riched20: ITextPara duplicates, comparison, CanChange and Reset

ITextPara::GetDuplicate returns a copy of the paragraph format that belongs to
no paragraph (changing either leaves the other alone), SetDuplicate applies a
duplicate's defined values to the paragraphs of the range, IsEqual compares two
formats (S_OK / S_FALSE with tomTrue / tomFalse), CanChange is the range's
CanEdit (tomFalse in a read-only control; a duplicate can always change), and
Reset(tomDefault) gives the paragraphs the format of a new paragraph. The
merge of a partial format into a PARAFORMAT2 is now para_fmt_merge, shared by
the editor's para_set_fmt (unchanged behaviour) and the duplicates.

Gate: test/richepara2-gate.sh (3 mutants caught).
---
diff --git a/dlls/riched20/editor.h b/dlls/riched20/editor.h
index 6f6aaba..9202a96 100644
--- a/dlls/riched20/editor.h
+++ b/dlls/riched20/editor.h
@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@ void editor_get_selection_para_fmt( ME_TextEditor *editor, PARAFORMAT2 *fmt );
 void editor_mark_rewrap_all( ME_TextEditor *editor );
 void editor_set_default_para_fmt(ME_TextEditor *editor, PARAFORMAT2 *pFmt);
 BOOL editor_set_selection_para_fmt( ME_TextEditor *editor, const PARAFORMAT2 *fmt );
+BOOL para_fmt_merge( PARAFORMAT2 *fmt, const PARAFORMAT2 *pFmt );
 void ME_MakeFirstParagraph(ME_TextEditor *editor, HDC hdc);
 void ME_DumpParaStyle(ME_Paragraph *s);
